HPLIP 3.25.2
https://sourceforge.net/projects/hplip/files/hplip/3.25.2/hplip-3.25.2.tar.gz

Files are copied from prnt/hpcups/ in the tarball, except the HPLIP
shared libraries libImageProcessor-x86_32.so and libImageProcessor-x86_64.so
(prebuilt binaries, not included). common/utils.c and common/utils.h live
in ../common/ as hplip_utils.c and hplip_utils.h.

Local changes to upstream sources:
- #include "utils.h" became #include "hplip_utils.h" in the .cpp files that
  use it (macOS file systems are case-insensitive and "utils.h" matched
  Utils.h in this directory).
- genPCLm.cpp includes "hplip_utils.h" instead of "./../../common/utils.h".
- jccolor.c is kept for reference but is not built (it needs libjpeg 6b
  private headers). src/compat/hp_csc.c redoes its Mojave and standard
  RGB to YCbCr tables, and ModeJpeg.cpp converts JetReady rows with it and
  passes YCbCr to libjpeg. tests/csc-check.c compares the two.
- ModeJbig.cpp no longer loads HP's plugin library (lj.so) and its
  hp_encode_bits_to_jbig symbol. It calls the built-in
  hp_encode_bits_to_jbig() from src/compat/hp_jbig.c, which uses jbigkit
  (src/jbigkit/). The function pointers HPLJJBGCompress and HPLJSoInit and
  the unload_library() call in the destructor are gone, and compressBuf is
  allocated at twice the raw size plus 4096 bytes so a JBIG stream that is
  larger than its input still fits.
- HPCupsFilter.cpp copies the job user name and title through
  copyJobField(), which replaces control characters, '"' and '\' (and '/'
  in the user name) with '_'. Both values come from the job submitter and
  go into quoted PJL strings and temp file names. The temp file names in
  HPCupsFilter.cpp and SystemServices.cpp use snprintf instead of sprintf.
- Hbpl1_Wrapper.cpp zero-initializes the PCLm page and user settings in
  StartPage() and sets srcColorSpaceSpefication to deviceRGB. Upstream left
  them uninitialized, and genPCLm.cpp read the source colour space from
  stack garbage (UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer, found by tests/fuzz).
- Mode9.cpp and Mode3.cpp test the byte count before reading the next byte
  in their run scans, so the last byte of a row no longer reads one past the
  row buffer (AddressSanitizer, found by make asan). Mode3.cpp counts the
  run in an unsigned int instead of a BYTE, so the loop compares like types.
- Mode10.cpp does the short-delta shift on unsigned values, and keeps the
  end-of-row sentinel to 24 bits so it cannot equal its neighbour and run
  the pixel scans off the row (UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer and tests/fuzz).
- ColorMatcher.cpp allocates 8 extra bytes after the contone planes. The
  halftoner pads each row to a multiple of 8 pixels and read that far past
  the buffer.
- Job.cpp rounds the unpacked black raster up to a multiple of 8 pixels,
  which unpackBits() writes.
- LJZjStream.cpp and LJZxStream.cpp copy the HPLJZjsJbgEncSt that follows
  the JBIG data into a local struct instead of reading it through an
  unaligned pointer.
- ModeJpeg.cpp declares output_buffer_callback with a size_t size, as
  jdatadbf.c calls it (call through a mismatched function type).
- ModeJbig.cpp refuses a page buffer over 512 MB. The ZjColor2 page height
  comes from the job and the size was computed in int.
- Lidil.cpp checks cupsInteger1 and cupsInteger2 before indexing the 5 x 5
  print mode maps.
- Hbpl1.cpp skips the remaining strips in FormFeed() when no strip buffer
  was allocated (a page with no raster rows).
- HPCupsFilter.cpp checks each page header before use (headerIsSane():
  colour space, enum fields, width, bits per pixel, bytes per line, page
  size and resolution ranges, and that later pages match the first), checks
  that the hbpl1 printable area fits the page and the read buffer, and
  stops the job when cupsRasterReadPixels() runs out of data. Found by
  tests/fuzz; upstream trusted every header field.
